---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy">
  <article class="legal"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1>Privacy, in plain language.</h1><p>Effective September 19, 2026</p>
    <h2>Where your organizer data lives</h2><p>Your maps and active-map selection are stored in your browser using local storage. Mapflowy does not upload this content to a server, and this release has no accounts or cross-device synchronization.</p>
    <h2>What leaves your browser</h2><p>The site host may receive standard web request information needed to deliver the website, such as your IP address, browser details, requested pages, and request times. Your map content is not included in those requests during normal use.</p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can edit or delete maps within the organizer, export an individual map as a JSON file, or remove all locally stored organizer data through your browser's site-data controls. Clearing site data, using another browser profile, or visiting the app under a different domain will not carry your maps with you.</p>
    <h2>Changes to this notice</h2><p>This notice will be updated before accounts, analytics, cloud synchronization, or any other collection of organizer content is introduced.</p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
